   "mechanism": "Known property of local linear matching at a narrow bandwidth. The local linear weights are unbounded when a treated unit has few distinct controls inside the bandwidth (0.06 on the score here), and a bootstrap resample, which repeats controls, makes that more likely. A handful of replications then land far from the rest and dominate the standard deviation of the bootstrap distribution: the mean reported SE is five times the sampling SD. On one sample, 60 resamples had a standard deviation of 0.18 and an interquartile scale of 0.12, against a sampling SD of 0.16; the gap to a mean SE of 0.80 is a few draws with extreme replications. Not rerun at a larger B (13 minutes per 200 draws; a ratio of 5 is not a Monte Carlo accident). The estimator now warns when the bootstrap standard deviation is more than twice the scale its interquartile range implies and reports that scale in model_info['bootstrap_se_iqr']. A wider bandwidth removes the problem (match.att.llr.wide)."
